WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.776
New York, June 1800.

00:00:05.836 --> 00:00:11.488
It's seven o'clock on a warm summer morning.

00:00:11.548 --> 00:00:14.648
A ship is arriving in New York.

00:00:14.708 --> 00:00:18.909
Its name is the Red Rose.

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:25.491
Two of the people on it are Sam Tinker and his daughter Jenny.

00:00:25.551 --> 00:00:28.644
Sam and Jenny are English.

00:00:28.704 --> 00:00:33.440
But now they are starting a new life in America.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:37.351
Look, Dad! says Jenny.
 
00:00:37.411 --> 00:00:39.242
We’re here!

00:00:39.302 --> 00:00:42.213
We’re really here!

00:00:42.274 --> 00:00:46.376
The Tinkers say goodbye to all their friends.

00:00:46.436 --> 00:00:51.248
Then they leave the Red Rose.

00:00:51.308 --> 00:00:58.660
There are lots of people, horses and carts beside the ship.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:01.220
Sam looks at them.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:06.122
Yes, we’re here, he thinks.
 
00:01:06.182 --> 00:01:08.544
But now what?

00:01:08.604 --> 00:01:11.596
We haven’t got any money.

00:01:11.655 --> 00:01:16.088
He stops a young man with a green coat.

00:01:16.148 --> 00:01:19.870
Excuse me, he says.
 
00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:22.952
I’m looking for a job.

00:01:23.012 --> 00:01:26.430
The man turns to his right.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:31.660
Talk to Jack Crane, he answers.
 
00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:34.532
Jack Crane is a farmer.

00:01:34.592 --> 00:01:42.038
He has a long, thin face and only three fingers on his right hand.

00:01:42.098 --> 00:01:45.770
He listens to Sam's story.

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:48.883
Then he takes off his hat.

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:56.092
OK, he says, you can both have jobs.
 
00:01:56.152 --> 00:02:00.550
I need a new man to work in the fields. 

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:05.265
And we want someone to help in the kitchen, too –

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:07.727
isn’t that right, Blue Sky?

00:02:07.747 --> 00:02:13.772
There's an Indian girl on top of the cart.

00:02:13.832 --> 00:02:21.318
Yes, she says, and smiles at Jenny.

00:02:21.378 --> 00:02:30.606
Two hours later, the Tinkers leave New York with Jack Crane and Blue Sky.

00:02:30.666 --> 00:02:33.616
They're both very happy.

00:02:33.676 --> 00:02:38.237
How far is it to your farm, Mr Crane?

00:02:38.297 --> 00:02:40.858
asks Sam.

00:02:40.918 --> 00:02:47.399
Eighty kilometres, Jack Crane answers.
 
00:02:47.459 --> 00:02:51.450
They drive all afternoon.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:54.524
Jenny is sitting next to Sam.

00:02:54.584 --> 00:02:59.089
She is tired, but she does not want to sleep.

00:02:59.149 --> 00:03:03.420
This is America, she thinks,

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:07.230
… and now I’m American.

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:12.552
After six hours, Jack Crane stops the cart.

00:03:12.612 --> 00:03:21.650
Well … there it is, he says. Jenny stands up.
 
00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:26.960
It's evening now, and the sun's going down.

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:35.188
In front of them, there are lots of beautiful yellow fields and a big farmhouse.

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:38.480
Jenny looks to her left.

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:42.054
Where’s that smoke coming from?

00:03:42.114 --> 00:03:44.255
she asks.

00:03:44.315 --> 00:03:47.878
That’s the Indian village,

00:03:47.938 --> 00:03:50.276
answers Blue Sky.

00:03:50.336 --> 00:03:54.772
My family lives there.

00:03:54.832 --> 00:04:00.154
The next day, the Tinkers start work.

00:04:00.214 --> 00:04:04.234
Jenny helps Blue Sky in the farmhouse.

00:04:04.294 --> 00:04:09.436
First, the two girls cook everyone's breakfast.

00:04:09.496 --> 00:04:12.916
Then they make all the beds.

00:04:12.976 --> 00:04:21.782
After that, they clean the kitchen floor.

00:04:21.842 --> 00:04:30.980
At the same time, Sam is working in the fields.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:37.075
After four or five hours, he stops for a minute.

00:04:37.135 --> 00:04:40.558
What are you stopping for?

00:04:40.618 --> 00:04:43.080
asks Jack Crane.

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:46.893
Come on – get back to work!
 
00:04:46.952 --> 00:04:53.975
Sam and Jenny have only one free day every week – Sunday.
 
00:04:54.034 --> 00:04:57.603
It's Blue Sky's free day too.

00:04:57.663 --> 00:05:01.394
That's when she visits her family.

00:05:01.453 --> 00:05:05.614
One Sunday, Jenny goes with her.

00:05:05.674 --> 00:05:09.336
She makes a lot of new friends.

00:05:09.395 --> 00:05:15.047
She meets the village Chief, too – Silver Cloud.

00:05:15.107 --> 00:05:20.378
He has a beautiful wife and a young son.

00:05:20.438 --> 00:05:26.272
After that first visit, Jenny often goes to the village.

00:05:26.332 --> 00:05:30.953
She starts to learn some Indian words too.

00:05:31.013 --> 00:05:35.700
Jenny is always happy with her new Indian friends, 

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:39.645
but she is not happy on the farm.

00:05:39.705 --> 00:05:43.096
Sam is unhappy, too.

00:05:43.156 --> 00:05:48.508
I don’t want to work here on Jack Crane’s farm any more,

00:05:48.568 --> 00:05:51.059
he says one evening.

00:05:51.119 --> 00:05:56.411
I want to work on my farm – Tinkers Farm.
 
00:05:56.471 --> 00:06:00.462
I know, Dad, Jenny answers.
 
00:06:00.522 --> 00:06:04.412
Then she thinks, But how?
 
00:06:04.472 --> 00:06:07.173
We can’t buy any land.

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:11.734
Jack Crane pays us only two dollars a week.

00:06:11.794 --> 00:06:17.794
Four days later, Jenny and Blue Sky are making the beds.

00:06:17.854 --> 00:06:21.311
Suddenly, they hear something.

00:06:21.371 --> 00:06:24.449
Two men are shouting.

00:06:24.509 --> 00:06:27.672
Jenny looks out of the window.

00:06:27.732 --> 00:06:33.506
She can see Jack Crane and her father in front of the farmhouse.

00:06:33.566 --> 00:06:37.670
Jack Crane's face is very red.

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:42.194
Do it! he shouts.
 
00:06:42.254 --> 00:06:46.126
No, I’m not going to!
 
00:06:46.186 --> 00:06:48.445
Sam shouts back.

00:06:48.505 --> 00:06:53.143
It’s Sunday and I don’t work on Sundays.

00:06:53.203 --> 00:06:54.913
You do it!

00:06:54.973 --> 00:06:59.024
Jenny runs downstairs and out of the house.

00:06:59.084 --> 00:07:03.444
There is a strong wind and it is raining.

00:07:03.504 --> 00:07:06.015
What’s happening?

00:07:06.075 --> 00:07:08.785
she asks her father.

00:07:08.845 --> 00:07:11.766
We’re leaving in the morning,

00:07:11.826 --> 00:07:13.936
Sam answers.

00:07:13.996 --> 00:07:16.977
He's walking very fast.

00:07:17.037 --> 00:07:19.232
Jenny looks at him.

00:07:19.292 --> 00:07:23.001
But … how are we going to eat?

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:26.192
We haven’t got any money.

00:07:26.252 --> 00:07:29.054
Sam doesn't answer.

00:07:29.114 --> 00:07:32.636
His eyes are cold and hard.

00:07:32.696 --> 00:07:39.052
That evening, Jenny and Blue Sky go to the Indian village.

00:07:39.112 --> 00:07:45.766
This is going to be my last visit, Jenny thinks.

00:07:45.826 --> 00:07:49.059
Blue Sky is sad, too.

00:07:49.119 --> 00:07:52.642
She doesn't want to lose her friend.

00:07:52.702 --> 00:07:57.154
The two girls say nothing for twenty minutes.

00:07:57.214 --> 00:08:01.368
Then Blue Sky stops her horse.

00:08:01.428 --> 00:08:05.641
She can see something in the river to their right.

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:09.042
It's a small boy.

00:08:09.102 --> 00:08:13.726
Help! he is shouting.
 
00:08:13.786 --> 00:08:20.707
I can’t swim! Help me! Please!
 
00:08:20.767 --> 00:08:25.408
It’s the Chief’s son! says Blue Sky.

00:08:25.468 --> 00:08:28.039
What are we going to do?

00:08:28.099 --> 00:08:34.140
But before she can say another word, Jenny gets off her horse.

00:08:34.201 --> 00:08:38.442
I’m coming! she shouts.
 
00:08:38.502 --> 00:08:42.433
Then she jumps into the cold river.

00:08:42.493 --> 00:08:47.138
Help! shouts the boy.
 
00:08:47.198 --> 00:08:49.642
Jenny swims to him.

00:08:49.702 --> 00:08:53.186
His head is going under the water.

00:08:53.246 --> 00:08:56.909
She puts one arm around him.

00:08:56.969 --> 00:09:00.982
It’s OK, she says.

00:09:01.042 --> 00:09:04.145
You’re safe now.

00:09:04.205 --> 00:09:11.531
Half an hour later, Jenny and Blue Sky arrive at the Indian village.

00:09:11.591 --> 00:09:14.846
The chief comes to meet them.

00:09:14.906 --> 00:09:22.144
But I don’t understand, he says to Blue Sky.

00:09:22.204 --> 00:09:25.316
Why is my son with you?

00:09:25.376 --> 00:09:30.411
And why are he and the English girl wet?

00:09:30.471 --> 00:09:34.954
Blue Sky tells him the story.

00:09:35.014 --> 00:09:39.688
After that, the chief's very happy.

00:09:39.748 --> 00:09:42.660
He smiles at Jenny.

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:47.442
How can I thank you? he says.
 
00:09:47.502 --> 00:09:54.486
Please, let me give you something. Anything.
 
00:09:54.546 --> 00:10:01.570
At nine o'clock, Sam's putting some boots into a bag.

00:10:01.630 --> 00:10:07.582
What’s going to happen tomorrow? he thinks.
 
00:10:07.642 --> 00:10:12.508
Suddenly, the door opens.

00:10:12.568 --> 00:10:15.874
It's Jenny.

00:10:15.934 --> 00:10:18.654
Come with me, Dad,

00:10:18.714 --> 00:10:23.546
she says. I want to show you something.

00:10:23.606 --> 00:10:26.637
Sam looks at his daughter.

00:10:26.698 --> 00:10:31.630
Her eyes are bright and she's smiling.

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:36.400
What are you talking about? he asks.
 
00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:41.150
There isn’t time for any questions, says Jenny.

00:10:41.532 --> 00:10:43.220
Come on.

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:46.898
She takes her father to a hill.

00:10:46.959 --> 00:10:51.120
At the top, she says, Look!

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:54.952
Can you see that land over there?

00:10:55.012 --> 00:11:00.004
Yes, Sam answers.

00:11:00.064 --> 00:11:05.176
Then Jenny tells him about Silver Cloud's son.

00:11:05.236 --> 00:11:13.700
After she finishes, Sam says, You mean …? Yes!
 
00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:17.176
Jenny smiles at her father.

00:11:17.236 --> 00:11:24.811
The Indians are giving us our own farm – Tinkers Farm.
 
00:11:24.831 --> 00:11:30.344
Oh Dad, isn’t it wonderful?

00:11:30.404 --> 00:11:34.576
Now we can really start a new life!